# Invariant 7: mls.commit_needed goes to the lowest-index online device, a 2-second watchdog moves
# the election on, and a device that ACKNOWLEDGES three rounds and commits none of them is removed
# by an instance Remove. Alice is the only member online when the instance kicks carol; she acks
# each round and does nothing, the clock moves 2 s past each deadline, and after the third lost
# round the instance proposes removing alice. Bob, back online, commits both Removes, and the
# instance no longer counts alice a member: once she has processed her own removal, even her fork
# report is answered as a stranger's.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group chat kind=text target=d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9d9 community=none creator=alice
join bob chat via=welcome
join carol chat via=welcome
sync bob
go_offline bob
go_offline carol
kick alice carol
ack_commit alice
advance_clock 2s
ack_commit alice
advance_clock 2s
ack_commit alice
advance_clock 2s
go_online bob
sync bob
commit bob
sync alice
expect_reject E_NOT_FOUND fork_report alice chat
